@@ -3,3 +3,17 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+resolvePointer({ a: { "b/c": [10, 20] } }, "/a/b~1c/1"); // 20
+resolvePointer(doc, ""); // the whole document
+```
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the referenced value. It throws a `JsonPointerError` when the
+pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer, or when it does not resolve to a value (missing member, array index
+out of range or `-`, or a step into a string, number, boolean or `null`). Only own members of objects are
+looked up. The URI fragment form (`#/a/b`) and modifying documents are not supported.
