+## Why
+
+Our services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer) is that standard, and later features of the toolkit will build on it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, which returns the value an RFC 6901 pointer refers to.
+- It throws when the pointer is not syntactically valid, or when it does not resolve to a value of the document.
+- Add the first source file, tests, and a `tsconfig`-compatible layout (`src/`), since the repository has no code yet.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: parsing and resolving RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+<!-- none -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code in `src/` and tests; public API of the library gains one function.
+- No dependencies added.
+- Out of scope: the URI fragment representation (`#/a/b`), and setting, adding or removing values.
