+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Pointer syntax
+A JSON Pointer SHALL be either the empty string or a sequence of one or more segments, each made of `/` followed by zero or more characters. Within a segment, `~` SHALL only appear as `~0` (meaning `~`) or `~1` (meaning `/`). Any other pointer, including any non-string value, SHALL be rejected with an error.
+
+#### Scenario: Pointer not starting with a slash
+- **WHEN** the pointer is `a/b`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Invalid escape
+- **WHEN** the pointer is `/a~2b` or `/a~`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Non-string pointer
+- **WHEN** the pointer is `undefined`, a number, or `null`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Whole-document reference
+The empty pointer SHALL resolve to the whole document.
+
+#### Scenario: Empty pointer
+- **WHEN** the pointer is `""`
+- **THEN** the document itself is returned, whatever its type (including `null` and primitives)
+
+### Requirement: Object member resolution
+A segment applied to an object SHALL resolve to the value of the member whose name equals the unescaped segment. Only the object's own members count; the empty string is a valid member name.
+
+#### Scenario: Nested members
+- **WHEN** the document is `{"a":{"b":1}}` and the pointer is `/a/b`
+- **THEN** `1` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Escaped names
+- **WHEN** the document is `{"a/b":1,"m~n":2}` and the pointers are `/a~1b` and `/m~0n`
+- **THEN** `1` and `2` are returned respectively
+
+#### Scenario: Escape order
+- **WHEN** the document is `{"~1":1,"/":2}` and the pointers are `/~01` and `/~1`
+- **THEN** `1` and `2` are returned respectively
+
+#### Scenario: Empty member name
+- **WHEN** the document is `{"":1}` and the pointer is `/`
+- **THEN** `1` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Missing member
+- **WHEN** the pointer names a member the object does not have
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Inherited names are not members
+- **WHEN** the pointer is `/__proto__`, `/constructor` or `/toString` and the object has no such own member
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Array element resolution
+A segment applied to an array SHALL resolve to the element at that zero-based index. The segment MUST be `0` or a digit sequence without leading zeros. The segment `-` (the element after the last) and any index past the end SHALL NOT resolve to a value.
+
+#### Scenario: Valid index
+- **WHEN** the document is `["a","b"]` and the pointer is `/1`
+- **THEN** `"b"` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Invalid index forms
+- **WHEN** the pointer is `/01`, `/+1`, `/-1`, `/1.0`, or `/x` against an array
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Index out of range or `-`
+- **WHEN** the document is `["a"]` and the pointer is `/1` or `/-`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Primitives have no children
+A segment applied to a string, number, boolean or `null` SHALL NOT resolve to a value.
+
+#### Scenario: Descending into a primitive
+- **WHEN** the document is `{"a":"text"}` and the pointer is `/a/0` or `/a/length`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: Existing values include null and falsy values
+A pointer to a member or element holding `null`, `false`, `0` or `""` SHALL return that value.
+
+#### Scenario: Null value
+- **WHEN** the document is `{"a":null}` and the pointer is `/a`
+- **THEN** `null` is returned
