+# json-pointer Specification
+
+## Purpose
+Resolve RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document, rejecting invalid pointers and pointers that do not refer to a value.
+
+## Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Pointer syntax
+A JSON Pointer SHALL be either the empty string or a sequence of one or more segments, each made of `/` followed by zero or more characters. Within a segment, `~` SHALL only appear as `~0` (meaning `~`) or `~1` (meaning `/`). Any other pointer, including any non-string value, SHALL be rejected with an error.
